ged budget risk on externally-funded scheme affects council's ability to deliver town regeneration commitments within available funding.","iso":"2026-09-08","paper_title":"Appendix 2 Financial Performance 2026-27 Q1","paper_url":"https://democracy.broxtowe.gov.uk/documents/s43473/43473.pdf","byline":"PWLBintel \u00b7 from committee papers","draft":true},{"headline":"Housing structural repairs budget at risk due to legacy issues and case volumes","lead":"Structural defects are not discretionary spending; unbudgeted costs cannot be deferred and may force reductions elsewhere.","iso":"2026-09-08","paper_title":"Appendix 2 Financial Performance 2026-27 Q1","paper_url":"https://democracy.broxtowe.gov.uk/documents/s43473/43473.pdf","byline":"PWLBintel \u00b7 from committee papers","draft":true}],"findings":[{"iso":"2026-09-08","committee":"Cabinet","paper_title":"Appendix 2 Financial Performance 2026-27 Q1","paper_url":"https://democracy.broxtowe.gov.uk/documents/s43473/43473.pdf","headline":"Pay award cost pressure of \u00a367k if 3.3% uplift accepted against 3% budget assumption","detail":"The 2026-27 budget assumed 3% pay inflation, but National Employers offered 3.3% on 2 June 2026. The offer remains unaccepted by unions. If accepted, the council quantifies the additional cost as 'around \u00a367k' for the year.","category":"overspend","matters":"Unbudgeted pay inflation is a direct hit to the bottom line with no mitigation identified; represents unfunded cost pressure.","figures":"\u00a367k impact if 3.3% accepted; 0.3 percentage point difference from budgeted 3%","quote":"If this pay award is accepted later, the overall impact on the budget for the year would be around \u00a367k.","material":true},{"iso":"2026-09-08","committee":"Cabinet","paper_title":"Appendix 2 Financial Performance 2026-27 Q1","paper_url":"https://democracy.broxtowe.gov.uk/documents/s43473/43473.pdf","headline":"Stapleford Towns Fund street improvement scheme flagged with explicit budget risk to completion","detail":"Early 2027 completion target with project designs underway and public consultation in September. The council explicitly notes that 'budget remains a risk until completion,' suggesting the full scope or timeline could drive costs above the allocated budget within the multi-year scheme.","category":"capital","matters":"Acknowledged budget risk on externally-funded scheme affects council's ability to deliver town regeneration commitments within available funding.","figures":"Part of Stapleford Towns Fund (\u00a35.713m approved), target completion early 2027","quote":"Project to complete early 2027, although budget remains a risk until completion.","material":true},{"iso":"2026-09-08","committee":"Cabinet","paper_title":"Appendix 2 Financial Performance 2026-27 Q1","paper_url":"https://democracy.broxtowe.gov.uk/documents/s43473/43473.pdf","headline":"Housing structural repairs budget at risk due to legacy issues and case volumes","detail":"At 28% spend in Q1 (\u00a356k of \u00a3200k), the council flags 'some risk with budget due to number of cases and legacy issues.' Legacy property defects are harder to predict and potentially cost more than anticipated.","category":"capital","matters":"Structural defects are not discretionary spending; unbudgeted costs cannot be deferred and may force reductions elsewhere.","figures":"\u00a3200k budget, \u00a356k spent to 30 June 2026","quote":"Structural Remedial Repairs: 200 56 In progress. Some risk with budget due to number of cases and legacy issues.","material":true},{"iso":"2026-09-08","committee":"Cabinet","paper_title":"Appendix 2 Financial Performance 2026-27 Q1","paper_url":"https://democracy.broxtowe.gov.uk/documents/s43473/43473.pdf","headline":"Housing damp proofing programme 50% spent by end of Q1 with acknowledged budget risk","detail":"The damp proofing works have consumed \u00a375k of a \u00a3150k annual budget in just three months, with the council noting risk 'with half of budget already spent.' This pace of spending suggests potential year-end budget exhaustion.","category":"capital","matters":"Rapid budget consumption in Q1 signals potential underfunding of housing condition works, requiring scope reduction or additional allocation mid-year.","figures":"\u00a3150k budget, \u00a375k spent (50%), within first three months of financial year","quote":"Damp Proofing Works: 150 75 In progress. Some risks with half of budget already spent.","material":true},{"iso":"2026-09-08","committee":"Cabinet","paper_title":"Appendix 2 Financial Performance 2026-27 Q1","paper_url":"https://democracy.broxtowe.gov.uk/documents/s43473/43473.pdf","headline":"Brinsley Headstocks refurbishment costs flagged as likely to exceed \u00a3137k budget","detail":"The procurement stage for this scheme is in its final stage, with the council explicitly noting that costs are likely to exceed the approved budget. No spend has yet occurred in Q1.","category":"capital","matters":"Cost overruns on approved capital schemes require finding additional funding or cutting other priorities, affecting overall capital delivery.","figures":"\u00a3137k budget, \u00a30 spent to 30 June 2026","quote":"Refurbishment of Brinsley Headstocks: 137 - Final stage of procurement underway, costs are likely to exceed budget.","material":true}],"editorial":null,"freshness":{"last_paper_iso":"2026-09-08"},"name":"Broxtowe","daily_post":{"iso":"2026-09-17","since_iso":"2026-08-18","distress":false,"headline":"Pay award cost pressure of \u00a367k if 3.3% uplift accepted against 3% budget assumption","lead":"Unbudgeted pay inflation is a direct hit to the bottom line with no mitigation identified; represents unfunded cost pressure.","also":["4 other findings in this window"],"watch":"Governance, Audit and Standards Committee on 2026-09-21","n_findings":5,"n_documents":0,"top_paper_title":"Appendix 2 Financial Performance 2026-27 Q1","top_paper_url":"https://democracy.broxtowe.gov.uk/documents/s43473/43473.pdf","draft":true},"findings_total":58,"news_drafts_total":3}}